1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,000
Advanced Class

2
00:00:02,090 --> 00:00:02,980
Next up...

3
00:00:03,480 --> 00:00:06,260
Wakaba, who's moved up 
to the advanced class.

4
00:00:06,750 --> 00:00:07,590
Yes.

5
00:00:08,250 --> 00:00:10,440
My name is Aoi Wakaba.

6
00:00:10,440 --> 00:00:14,620
I'm an elf hailing from Liefgard, 
a now-bygone treetop city.

7
00:00:15,030 --> 00:00:17,260
A treetop city?

8
00:00:17,260 --> 00:00:19,660
Where is that, Mr. Hitoma?

9
00:00:19,660 --> 00:00:22,310
I don't know, either.

10
00:00:22,760 --> 00:00:28,320
The reason I want to be human 
is to let everyone know of my beauty.

11
00:00:29,040 --> 00:00:33,640
I'll become number one in the 
human world, not just in Liefgard.

12
00:00:34,080 --> 00:00:35,990
Wonderful, don't you think?

13
00:00:35,990 --> 00:00:37,680
Huh? Sure...

14
00:00:37,680 --> 00:00:39,770
She sure is confident in herself.

15
00:00:39,770 --> 00:00:43,830
Prince Waka was like this all the time
in the intermediate class, too.

16
00:00:46,300 --> 00:00:48,880
Now for... Okonogi.

17
00:00:49,650 --> 00:00:51,000
Got it.

18
00:00:51,000 --> 00:00:54,290
I'm Maki Okonogi.

19
00:00:54,290 --> 00:00:56,520
I'm descended from oni.

20
00:00:57,190 --> 00:01:00,710
The reason I wanna be human...

21
00:01:00,710 --> 00:01:01,940
Um...

22
00:01:01,940 --> 00:01:04,090
I forgot.

23
00:01:04,380 --> 00:01:05,480
What?

24
00:01:07,670 --> 00:01:09,150
That was a lie.

25
00:01:09,580 --> 00:01:10,760
You were lying?

26
00:01:10,760 --> 00:01:18,200
The reason I wanna be human 
is because I don't wanna lie.

27
00:01:18,890 --> 00:01:21,080
Because you don't want to lie?

28
00:01:21,500 --> 00:01:23,260
Listen up, Okonogi.

29
00:01:23,610 --> 00:01:26,190
Not all humans are good people.

30
00:01:26,850 --> 00:01:28,980
There are plenty of humans who lie.

31
00:01:29,450 --> 00:01:33,820
But you want to become human 
just so that you don't lie?

32
00:01:33,820 --> 00:01:38,180
Really? Then I don't wanna.

33
00:01:38,610 --> 00:01:39,290
Huh?

34
00:01:39,830 --> 00:01:41,790
That's a lie.

35
00:01:43,640 --> 00:01:48,650
I'm an honest liar.

36
00:01:48,650 --> 00:01:50,300
Is that right?

37
00:01:50,970 --> 00:01:52,500
Sure, okay.

38
00:01:53,750 --> 00:01:55,570
Let's work hard until you graduate.

39
00:01:55,570 --> 00:01:57,010
Sure thing.

40
00:01:58,330 --> 00:02:01,560
Did you really understand it, Mr. Hitoma?

41
00:02:01,900 --> 00:02:04,670
What Miss Okonogi said earlier.

42
00:02:05,170 --> 00:02:05,920
Yep.

43
00:02:05,920 --> 00:02:08,670
I get now that 
I don't understand her at all.

44
00:02:08,670 --> 00:02:10,070
Huh?

45
00:02:11,470 --> 00:02:16,480
The director let her enroll as a student, 
so she must have a good reason.

46
00:02:17,430 --> 00:02:19,010
Let's take our time getting to know her.

47
00:02:20,530 --> 00:02:21,550
Yes!

48
00:03:52,190 --> 00:03:56,990
Episode 12

49
00:03:52,190 --> 00:03:56,990
Episode 12

50
00:03:52,190 --> 00:03:56,990
The Misanthrope and Falsehood Found Nigh

51
00:03:52,190 --> 00:03:56,990
The Misanthrope and Falsehood Found Nigh

52
00:03:52,960 --> 00:03:56,080
What was it you wanted 
to discuss, Mr. Hitoma?

53
00:03:56,080 --> 00:04:00,130
Haneda, was it your idea 
to have Haruna work here?

54
00:04:01,850 --> 00:04:03,850
That's really only half right.

55
00:04:04,230 --> 00:04:05,520
Half?

56
00:04:06,200 --> 00:04:08,940
All I did was provide her with the chance.

57
00:04:09,310 --> 00:04:12,360
Ms. Haruna was the one 
who took it of her own will.

58
00:04:12,360 --> 00:04:15,770
Just as you did when you chose our school.

59
00:04:16,350 --> 00:04:19,640
Haneda, what is it you want from us?

60
00:04:19,640 --> 00:04:21,150
Nothing in particular.

61
00:04:22,320 --> 00:04:26,770
If you perform your duties 
as teachers, that's all I need.

62
00:04:26,770 --> 00:04:31,490
You and Ms. Haruna may share a past, 
but she doesn't seem to begrudge you.

63
00:04:32,060 --> 00:04:34,500
Or so she says, anyway...

64
00:04:34,690 --> 00:04:36,940
Isn't that for the best, then?

65
00:04:36,940 --> 00:04:41,130
I'd like nothing better than for you to 
work together to guide our students.

66
00:04:41,130 --> 00:04:42,940
Including me.

67
00:04:42,940 --> 00:04:44,050
You as well?

68
00:04:44,230 --> 00:04:48,700
I want to graduate one day 
and become human, too.

69
00:04:48,700 --> 00:04:50,120
I really mean it.

70
00:04:50,810 --> 00:04:53,550
So I'll be in your hands, Mr. Hitoma.

71
00:04:54,230 --> 00:04:57,440
Advanced Class

72
00:04:55,160 --> 00:04:57,440
Okay, I'm handing back your tests 
from the other day.

73
00:04:59,200 --> 00:05:00,820
Could be better.

74
00:05:01,280 --> 00:05:03,290
How'd you do, Maki?

75
00:05:03,290 --> 00:05:05,150
I got a perfect score.

76
00:05:05,150 --> 00:05:06,490
Seriously?!

77
00:05:06,490 --> 00:05:08,540
I was lying.

78
00:05:08,750 --> 00:05:10,420
What a stupid lie.

79
00:05:10,420 --> 00:05:13,940
I actually got a zero.

80
00:05:15,280 --> 00:05:17,920
I don't remember your grades 
being so poor, Maki.

81
00:05:18,110 --> 00:05:20,420
That was a lie.

82
00:05:20,420 --> 00:05:22,400
You had me worried.

83
00:05:22,860 --> 00:05:25,740
If you were telling the truth, 
you'd have to take remedial lessons.

84
00:05:27,190 --> 00:05:31,810
If I get a zero, I can be alone 
with Mr. Rei for remedial lessons?!

85
00:05:31,810 --> 00:05:33,150
Not happening.

86
00:05:33,640 --> 00:05:36,150
I'd leave it to Ms. Haruna 
if that happened.

87
00:05:38,880 --> 00:05:42,970
Miss Okonogi's still telling lots of lies.

88
00:05:43,420 --> 00:05:45,210
I'm used to it now, though.

89
00:05:45,760 --> 00:05:49,370
I think of it as a speech quirk now, 
so it doesn't bother me anymore.

90
00:05:49,370 --> 00:05:53,260
It really doesn't bother you, does it?

91
00:05:53,720 --> 00:05:55,360
When your students lie.

92
00:05:57,760 --> 00:05:59,090
Ms. Haruna.

93
00:05:59,090 --> 00:06:00,160
Yes?

94
00:06:01,310 --> 00:06:06,510
You're really fine with 
what happened back then?

95
00:06:08,270 --> 00:06:10,190
Are you just trying to 
put on a brave face?

96
00:06:12,120 --> 00:06:15,440
Can I say what's really on my mind?

97
00:06:17,440 --> 00:06:18,720
Mr. Hitoma.

98
00:06:19,260 --> 00:06:21,300
I'm angry at you.

99
00:06:22,810 --> 00:06:24,580
Didn't I tell you already?

100
00:06:24,580 --> 00:06:27,960
We should forget about what happened.

101
00:06:29,510 --> 00:06:32,070
We can't change the past.

102
00:06:32,070 --> 00:06:33,980
We can only look to the future.

103
00:06:34,690 --> 00:06:36,960
You know what my name is, right?

104
00:06:38,030 --> 00:06:40,880
Mirai Haruna.

105
00:06:40,880 --> 00:06:42,700
Mirai, as in "future."

106
00:06:43,050 --> 00:06:46,130
Let's just think about 
the future from here on out.

107
00:06:46,800 --> 00:06:49,560
Yeah, I guess...

108
00:06:49,560 --> 00:06:50,660
Okay!

109
00:06:53,730 --> 00:06:55,270
Final Exams

110
00:06:53,730 --> 00:06:55,270
1. Social Studies
 2. Japanese
 3. Math

111
00:07:06,010 --> 00:07:08,350
Enjoying some sun, Okonogi?

112
00:07:08,350 --> 00:07:09,830
It sure is warm out today.

113
00:07:10,230 --> 00:07:12,890
What? It's cold.

114
00:07:12,890 --> 00:07:16,250
Oh, I guess it's chilly with the wind.

115
00:07:16,250 --> 00:07:18,180
I was lying.

116
00:07:18,180 --> 00:07:20,330
I'm glad you weren't cold.

117
00:07:21,050 --> 00:07:22,830
Wouldn't want you getting sick.

118
00:07:22,830 --> 00:07:29,360
Mr. Hitoma, you don't seem to 
care that I'm a liar.

119
00:07:29,360 --> 00:07:30,440
You think?

120
00:07:30,440 --> 00:07:34,270
Yeah. You never get mad at me.

121
00:07:34,270 --> 00:07:37,360
It's not like your lies 
ever cause any trouble.

122
00:07:38,060 --> 00:07:39,780
There's no reason to be mad.

123
00:07:40,210 --> 00:07:42,590
Hey, Mr. Hitoma.

124
00:07:44,030 --> 00:07:47,230
You see, the truth is...

125
00:07:48,230 --> 00:07:51,450
I can tell when other people lie.

126
00:07:53,200 --> 00:07:56,910
Just kidding. That's a lie.

127
00:07:56,910 --> 00:07:58,730
You were lying?!

128
00:07:58,730 --> 00:08:01,560
I thought you might 
really have that ability.

129
00:08:06,700 --> 00:08:10,140
What were things like 
before you came here, Okonogi?

130
00:08:10,610 --> 00:08:15,060
Well, I was living with my mom.

131
00:08:15,610 --> 00:08:21,450
But well, back in grade school, 
some things got out of hand.

132
00:08:22,000 --> 00:08:25,230
And well, that's why I came here.

133
00:08:25,570 --> 00:08:29,450
Can you tell me a little more about that?

134
00:08:29,450 --> 00:08:36,140
Well, another girl in my class 
did something bad.

135
00:08:36,140 --> 00:08:39,450
And she told a lie to keep it secret.

136
00:08:39,450 --> 00:08:40,300
A lie?

137
00:08:41,250 --> 00:08:45,920
I pointed out that she was lying.

138
00:08:45,920 --> 00:08:51,540
Then they figured out 
that I could see through lies...

139
00:08:51,540 --> 00:08:54,370
Including some powerful people...

140
00:08:54,370 --> 00:08:59,430
And then my mom told me 
where to find this school.

141
00:08:59,630 --> 00:09:02,330
Okonogi, does that mean you really...

142
00:09:02,330 --> 00:09:03,610
Mr. Hitoma.

143
00:09:04,490 --> 00:09:06,190
Are you basking in the sun?

144
00:09:06,680 --> 00:09:14,060
You see, I was asking Mr. Hitoma 
for some advice.

145
00:09:14,840 --> 00:09:18,700
Mr. Hitoma's a wonderful 
and reliable teacher, isn't he?

146
00:09:19,500 --> 00:09:25,870
Ms. Mirai, you're a good, 
hardworking teacher, too.

147
00:09:26,220 --> 00:09:28,630
I'm happy to hear that 
you think of me that way!

148
00:09:31,630 --> 00:09:33,700
Crouch down!

149
00:09:34,110 --> 00:09:36,560
Like this?

150
00:09:38,650 --> 00:09:41,720
Now that's a good girl.

151
00:09:41,720 --> 00:09:45,330
Thank you very much...?

152
00:09:46,200 --> 00:09:51,210
Ms. Mirai, why'd you become a teacher?

153
00:09:56,460 --> 00:09:59,610
I wanted to become just like Mr. Hitoma.

154
00:10:03,790 --> 00:10:06,420
Hey, why don't we...

155
00:10:06,920 --> 00:10:09,170
all take a field trip sometime?

156
00:10:09,170 --> 00:10:10,830
A field trip?

157
00:10:10,830 --> 00:10:14,060
You mean a date outdoors with Mr. Rei?

158
00:10:14,060 --> 00:10:15,640
I'm pretty sure she doesn't.

159
00:10:17,170 --> 00:10:20,720
We do have hands-on lessons 
where we learn about the human world,

160
00:10:21,100 --> 00:10:23,810
but they all take place on school grounds.

161
00:10:23,810 --> 00:10:28,610
It's not the same as getting to interact 
with real humans outside the barrier.

162
00:10:28,610 --> 00:10:30,770
Sounds great!

163
00:10:30,770 --> 00:10:35,450
I want to try one of every 
convenience store's signature products!

164
00:10:35,450 --> 00:10:39,550
Are we even allowed 
to go outside the school?

165
00:10:39,550 --> 00:10:41,150
We did it two years ago.

166
00:10:41,600 --> 00:10:43,750
Playing by the river in the summer.

167
00:10:43,900 --> 00:10:47,250
That sounds nice! I'm so jealous!

168
00:10:47,480 --> 00:10:50,340
I wanna go play somewhere off-campus, too!

169
00:10:51,360 --> 00:10:52,840
Got it.

170
00:10:53,210 --> 00:10:57,740
There's a special off-campus permit within
two kilometers if you're with a teacher,

171
00:10:58,110 --> 00:11:00,150
so I'll ask the principal for one.

172
00:11:00,150 --> 00:11:05,360
But wouldn't it be bad if people 
found out about their true identities?

173
00:11:05,360 --> 00:11:06,190
It would.

174
00:11:06,190 --> 00:11:08,560
They could end up being expelled.

175
00:11:09,160 --> 00:11:12,110
I'm fine if I wear a hat to hide my ears.

176
00:11:12,110 --> 00:11:15,900
I can hide my tail with a long skirt!

177
00:11:16,190 --> 00:11:19,550
Miss Ryuzaki's tail 
seems like it'd be discovered.

178
00:11:19,550 --> 00:11:20,580
Not at all!

179
00:11:20,890 --> 00:11:23,060
I'll do my best to hide it with a coat!

180
00:11:23,410 --> 00:11:26,520
An outdoors Christmas date with Mr. Rei!

181
00:11:26,830 --> 00:11:29,580
I'll do anything to make sure it happens!

182
00:11:32,630 --> 00:11:34,140
Everyone's here?

183
00:11:34,140 --> 00:11:36,510
We're handing out the rings.

184
00:11:37,230 --> 00:11:39,340
Don't lose it by any means.

185
00:11:39,920 --> 00:11:42,040
You won't be able to get back if you do.

186
00:11:42,040 --> 00:11:43,460
Okay!

187
00:11:44,020 --> 00:11:46,020
Shiranui Shrine Stop

188
00:11:46,570 --> 00:11:48,920
Machi, you're gonna buy snacks?

189
00:11:48,920 --> 00:11:50,310
That's right!

190
00:11:50,490 --> 00:11:54,270
I can't forget to buy fresh pastries,
 which I usually can't try!

191
00:11:54,270 --> 00:11:57,610
I also want to eat some 
limited-time ice creams!

192
00:11:58,330 --> 00:12:00,360
What are you going to buy, Okonogi?

193
00:12:00,360 --> 00:12:04,700
Um... steamed red bean buns?

194
00:12:04,700 --> 00:12:06,200
Red bean buns?

195
00:12:06,870 --> 00:12:08,170
Great choice.

196
00:12:09,240 --> 00:12:09,920
<i>Huh?</i>

197
00:12:10,570 --> 00:12:12,780
What's up, Mr. Hitoma?

198
00:12:13,110 --> 00:12:14,240
Oh, nothing.

199
00:12:14,950 --> 00:12:17,720
I was thinking of grabbing a pizza bun.

200
00:12:19,420 --> 00:12:23,510
My mom loved red bean buns.

201
00:12:24,200 --> 00:12:26,400
We're almost at the convenience store.

202
00:12:26,400 --> 00:12:28,690
I'm getting nervous!

203
00:12:28,690 --> 00:12:31,400
Christmas Chicken

204
00:12:29,100 --> 00:12:31,400
So this is a convenience store!

205
00:12:31,720 --> 00:12:35,180
Oh, wow. They even have a Christmas tree.

206
00:12:35,180 --> 00:12:37,280
They do.

207
00:12:37,900 --> 00:12:39,480
Mr. Hitoma!

208
00:12:39,480 --> 00:12:41,580
Make sure you stay with me!

209
00:12:41,580 --> 00:12:42,870
Me, too!

210
00:12:42,870 --> 00:12:43,830
Hey, now!

211
00:12:43,980 --> 00:12:46,120
I wouldn't want to get lost!

212
00:12:46,120 --> 00:12:48,500
What if I end up getting stranded?

213
00:12:48,500 --> 00:12:49,920
What?

214
00:12:55,000 --> 00:12:58,670
Powder
Foundation

215
00:12:56,350 --> 00:12:58,670
Look at all of these makeup products!

216
00:12:58,850 --> 00:13:01,490
Let's hurry to the snack section!

217
00:13:01,490 --> 00:13:03,720
Go on by yourself first!

218
00:13:03,880 --> 00:13:06,250
I'm scared of ending up lost and alone!

219
00:13:06,250 --> 00:13:08,060
Mr. Hitoma, let's go!

220
00:13:08,060 --> 00:13:13,020
No! I need to see what colors 
Mr. Rei prefers out of these!

221
00:13:13,560 --> 00:13:17,020
Ms. Haruna, can you take care of Nezu?

222
00:13:13,970 --> 00:13:18,520
C'mon, Mr. Hitoma! Let's go!

223
00:13:17,330 --> 00:13:20,900
Okay, Miss Nezu. Come with me.

224
00:13:21,420 --> 00:13:23,820
Fine, I guess...

225
00:13:23,840 --> 00:13:26,100
Calpis
Water

226
00:13:23,840 --> 00:13:26,100
Calpis
Water

227
00:13:38,590 --> 00:13:39,650
What?!

228
00:13:42,630 --> 00:13:45,920
All of the stuff here's for sale, right?

229
00:13:45,920 --> 00:13:49,850
Yes. Everything with a price tag, that is.

230
00:13:49,850 --> 00:13:52,110
Can I touch them?

231
00:13:52,110 --> 00:13:56,310
You can, but try not to touch the ones 
you're not buying too much.

232
00:13:56,510 --> 00:13:58,730
Sure thing!

233
00:13:59,790 --> 00:14:01,690
Wakaba, looking at fashion magazines?

234
00:14:01,690 --> 00:14:04,830
Printed paper really is so nice.

235
00:14:04,830 --> 00:14:08,270
It feels so much more real than 
just reading it on your phone.

236
00:14:09,190 --> 00:14:12,670
These pages, too, are bursting 
with the essence of life.

237
00:14:13,760 --> 00:14:16,500
Although I'm more beautiful.

238
00:14:18,800 --> 00:14:20,340
Oh, that's right!

239
00:14:20,580 --> 00:14:22,510
I'm out of packing tape!

240
00:14:22,850 --> 00:14:24,830
And packaging twine!

241
00:14:25,260 --> 00:14:27,090
Is now the time to stock up on those?

242
00:14:27,800 --> 00:14:29,600
Huh? Where's Okonogi?

243
00:14:32,480 --> 00:14:35,310
Ryuzaki, can I ask you to wait right here?

244
00:14:35,310 --> 00:14:38,530
What? You'd leave me all alone?

245
00:14:38,530 --> 00:14:41,230
So you've grown tired of me?!

246
00:14:41,440 --> 00:14:43,970
No, not what I mean...

247
00:14:43,970 --> 00:14:47,160
What's wrong, Mr. Hitoma?

248
00:14:47,830 --> 00:14:50,380
Okonogi, where have you been?

249
00:14:50,380 --> 00:14:53,470
Huh? Right here all along.

250
00:14:53,950 --> 00:14:54,880
I see.

251
00:14:55,240 --> 00:14:58,740
Try not to leave my sight, 
or I'll be worried.

252
00:14:58,740 --> 00:15:01,840
I suppose I could consider the idea.

253
00:15:02,050 --> 00:15:04,850
Where'd you learn to talk like that?

254
00:15:05,520 --> 00:15:07,880
So? Decided on what to buy?

255
00:15:07,880 --> 00:15:09,570
A red bean bun.

256
00:15:09,570 --> 00:15:11,510
Right. Anything else?

257
00:15:11,510 --> 00:15:13,040
Nope.

258
00:15:13,040 --> 00:15:16,130
All I want is the red bean bun.

259
00:15:19,110 --> 00:15:22,760
I remember when shopping 
seemed like a big adventure as a kid.

260
00:15:22,760 --> 00:15:24,680
It sure did.

261
00:15:24,680 --> 00:15:26,320
Huh? Where's Maki?

262
00:15:26,680 --> 00:15:27,990
What?!

263
00:15:27,990 --> 00:15:29,220
Okonogi?!

264
00:15:29,220 --> 00:15:32,580
Did she get lost? Maki!

265
00:15:33,110 --> 00:15:34,160
I'll look for her.

266
00:15:34,540 --> 00:15:36,600
Ms. Haruna, keep an eye on the others.

267
00:15:36,600 --> 00:15:37,750
Of course!

268
00:15:37,970 --> 00:15:40,670
Okonogi! Okonogi!

269
00:15:44,770 --> 00:15:45,740
Okonogi!

270
00:15:46,870 --> 00:15:48,350
Mr. Hitoma...

271
00:15:48,350 --> 00:15:50,050
What's wrong, Okonogi?

272
00:15:50,950 --> 00:15:52,720
My red bean bun...

273
00:15:53,180 --> 00:15:55,640
I dropped it...

274
00:15:56,440 --> 00:15:58,320
That's too bad.

275
00:15:58,320 --> 00:16:05,790
I was chasing the bun after I dropped it, 
and then I lost sight of everyone.

276
00:16:05,790 --> 00:16:09,070
I see. Let's go buy another someday.

277
00:16:10,350 --> 00:16:11,780
Mr. Hitoma.

278
00:16:12,510 --> 00:16:16,250
Is my mom doing well?

279
00:16:16,250 --> 00:16:21,220
Sorry, I'm not privy to that information.

280
00:16:21,770 --> 00:16:24,870
You've always lived with your mom, right?

281
00:16:24,870 --> 00:16:26,560
I sure have.

282
00:16:26,560 --> 00:16:30,930
Is your mom, well... the same as you?

283
00:16:30,930 --> 00:16:37,080
Nope. My mom's a normal human.

284
00:16:37,690 --> 00:16:42,760
I guess one of my ancestors was an oni.

285
00:16:42,760 --> 00:16:45,380
Like what they call atavism?

286
00:16:45,380 --> 00:16:49,390
Sometimes, you end up with 
someone like me.

287
00:16:49,390 --> 00:16:54,620
Mom told me her grandma was like me, too.

288
00:16:55,630 --> 00:17:00,290
Someone who could see through lies.

289
00:17:00,290 --> 00:17:01,740
Okonogi...

290
00:17:03,260 --> 00:17:05,590
You can really tell when people are lying?

291
00:17:05,950 --> 00:17:09,860
Mr. Hitoma, you don't lie very much.

292
00:17:10,220 --> 00:17:10,910
What?

293
00:17:11,310 --> 00:17:15,320
If only more people could be like you.

294
00:17:15,320 --> 00:17:19,860
Then I could have lived with my mom.

295
00:17:20,630 --> 00:17:24,450
You didn't want to 
leave your mom, did you?

296
00:17:26,220 --> 00:17:34,160
But I didn't want to be taken somewhere 
scary, like my mom's grandma.

297
00:17:34,400 --> 00:17:35,740
Somewhere scary?

298
00:17:35,740 --> 00:17:39,540
I don't know the details, 
but that's what Mom told me.

299
00:17:40,300 --> 00:17:45,310
That's why I wanna be a human, like her.

300
00:17:45,310 --> 00:17:49,770
Then it'll be okay to live with her.

301
00:17:49,770 --> 00:17:50,900
Makes sense.

302
00:17:51,900 --> 00:17:54,550
But why do you lie all the time?

303
00:17:55,070 --> 00:17:57,660
Because I'm a bad person!

304
00:17:58,310 --> 00:17:59,290
That's a lie.

305
00:18:01,810 --> 00:18:10,740
I figured if I lied a lot, it'd be harder
to tell what was a lie and what wasn't.

306
00:18:11,190 --> 00:18:17,020
In the end, it's my fault 
for not being normal.

307
00:18:17,870 --> 00:18:19,520
You're lying again.

308
00:18:19,520 --> 00:18:21,060
Am I?

309
00:18:21,500 --> 00:18:24,060
You are. I can tell.

310
00:18:25,390 --> 00:18:27,540
Then maybe I am.

311
00:18:28,730 --> 00:18:31,480
So you can really see through lies.

312
00:18:33,270 --> 00:18:38,100
Well, I can see the colors 
of everyone's voices.

313
00:18:38,670 --> 00:18:42,180
Sometimes they're reddish, 
and sometimes they're bluish.

314
00:18:43,340 --> 00:18:45,900
Can you see my voice right now?

315
00:18:45,900 --> 00:18:49,040
Yep. It's on the bluish side.

316
00:18:49,480 --> 00:18:54,810
Usami's and Macchi's are 
mostly blue as well.

317
00:18:54,810 --> 00:18:58,070
Sometimes they're purple, though.

318
00:18:58,800 --> 00:19:02,430
Why did you tell me about this?

319
00:19:02,430 --> 00:19:06,180
You made me remember my mom.

320
00:19:06,570 --> 00:19:10,590
At first, her voice was mostly blue.

321
00:19:11,070 --> 00:19:17,010
But over time, it became redder 
whenever she talked about me.

322
00:19:18,040 --> 00:19:22,180
I couldn't help but feel sorry.

323
00:19:22,610 --> 00:19:28,860
Mr. Hitoma. Why do humans have to lie?

324
00:19:30,270 --> 00:19:34,380
It'd be better if they didn't.

325
00:19:34,720 --> 00:19:36,190
Lying, huh?

326
00:19:36,880 --> 00:19:38,530
It serves as protection, I guess.

327
00:19:38,840 --> 00:19:40,380
Protecting what?

328
00:19:40,380 --> 00:19:42,790
Yourself, or other people.

329
00:19:44,170 --> 00:19:46,810
So it's not your fault, Okonogi.

330
00:19:46,810 --> 00:19:47,630
Huh?

331
00:19:48,050 --> 00:19:54,410
Um, what I mean is that 
you're fine the way you are.

332
00:19:56,000 --> 00:19:58,920
You sure are nice.

333
00:19:58,920 --> 00:20:02,780
I wish I could be like you.

334
00:20:02,780 --> 00:20:05,450
Why would you want to become like me?

335
00:20:05,890 --> 00:20:09,150
Wouldn't Ms. Haruna be closer 
in terms of her age and tastes?

336
00:20:09,150 --> 00:20:10,620
That's true.

337
00:20:10,620 --> 00:20:14,660
Ms. Mirai's a lot more like me.

338
00:20:14,660 --> 00:20:19,000
Maybe that's why I admire you so much.

339
00:20:19,000 --> 00:20:19,700
Huh?

340
00:20:20,030 --> 00:20:24,990
I wonder what Ms. Mirai's 
trying to protect.

341
00:20:25,180 --> 00:20:25,890
What?

342
00:20:26,890 --> 00:20:31,750
People lie to protect 
something, don't they?

343
00:20:33,050 --> 00:20:34,800
Mr. Hitoma!

344
00:20:34,970 --> 00:20:36,770
I'm glad you're all right.

345
00:20:36,770 --> 00:20:38,720
I was so worried!

346
00:20:38,870 --> 00:20:43,640
I'm sorry! I was spacing out.

347
00:20:44,150 --> 00:20:49,060
<i>I wonder what Ms. Mirai's 
trying to protect.</i>

348
00:20:49,740 --> 00:20:54,230
<i>People lie to protect 
something, don't they?</i>

349
00:20:54,520 --> 00:20:56,430
Ms. Mirai!

350
00:20:56,430 --> 00:20:57,880
What is it?

351
00:20:57,880 --> 00:21:00,230
Can I pat your head?

352
00:21:00,230 --> 00:21:02,570
What? Again?

353
00:21:02,570 --> 00:21:04,110
Crouch down!

354
00:21:05,770 --> 00:21:07,540
All right.

355
00:21:08,410 --> 00:21:12,680
Ms. Mirai, you're a good girl.

356
00:21:12,680 --> 00:21:15,020
Don't be too hard on yourself.

357
00:21:16,650 --> 00:21:18,380
Can I give you a hug as well?

358
00:21:20,360 --> 00:21:22,210
Do as you like.

359
00:21:25,200 --> 00:21:27,300
Ms. Mirai.

360
00:21:27,720 --> 00:21:31,770
You're a big liar 
whenever it comes to Mr. Hitoma.

361
00:21:34,400 --> 00:21:35,280
What's wrong?

362
00:21:36,970 --> 00:21:40,900
I'll head back first and 
tell the principal what happened.

363
00:21:40,900 --> 00:21:42,180
Ms. Haruna!

364
00:21:42,180 --> 00:21:45,600
Okonogi, what did you say to Ms. Haruna?

365
00:21:47,290 --> 00:21:51,910
I don't think you'd 
understand, Mr. Hitoma.

366
00:21:54,710 --> 00:21:57,490
Since you're bluish.

367
00:21:57,850 --> 00:22:02,460
You'd only get it if you were 
pure red, like the two of us.

368
00:23:33,060 --> 00:23:40,250
Next Episode:

369
00:23:33,060 --> 00:23:40,250
The Misanthrope and the Nigh Future

